  "caveats": {
   "parlay": "Combined probability multiplies the legs, which assumes the fights are independent; they are not quite. Backtested on the confirm period, 3-leg parlays returned +21.6% over 224 parlays - promising but about 1.5 standard deviations, and those parlays share legs, so this is NOT an established edge.",
   "profiles": "The market is hard to beat in MMA, and a parlay pays the bookmaker's margin once for every leg. These are the likeliest tickets that reach each payout, not bets expected to profit. Backtested point in time, one ticket a card, from 2023-11-01 to 2026-08-08: ~5x (mixed, else steady): 90 tickets, 12 won, -38% a ticket (-69% to -7%), paying x4.59 at the median (x4.50 to x6.15); ~10x: 75 tickets, 8 won, +8% a ticket (-58% to +84%), paying x9.78 at the median (x9.52 to x11.7); 50-100x: 36 tickets, 0 won, -100% a ticket (-100% to -100%), paying x51.9 at the median (x50.1 to x71.2). A 50-100x ticket landed 0 times in 36. An interval that spans zero is no evidence of an edge. Multipliers use the best price seen across the books on file, so one book may pay less than shown. Method props (KO, submission) are not priced live: every leg is a moneyline, and a finishing route is the reason, not the bet. Combined chances multiply the legs, which assumes the fights are independent."
  },
